---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title={`About ${site.name} | REALTOR® Flower Mound`} description="Meet Diego Alvarado — investor-turned-REALTOR® with Monument Realty serving Flower Mound and North DFW. Hablo Español.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Diego Alvarado</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">
          REALTOR® with {site.brokerage}, serving buyers, sellers, relocators, and investors across
          Flower Mound and the North DFW suburbs. Hablo Español.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="portrait-card">
        <div class="photo-placeholder">
          <div>
            <div class="label">Headshot coming soon</div>
            <div class="name">{site.name}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>From investor to REALTOR®</h2>
      <p>
        Diego’s path into real estate started on the investment side — learning deals, renovations,
        and property operations — before earning his Texas real estate license in April 2024
        (License #{site.license}). That sequence matters: it is why conversations tend to include
        numbers, contingencies, and second-order risks, not just listing photos.
      </p>
      <h2>Who he works with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>First-time and move-up buyers comparing North DFW suburbs</li>
        <li>Sellers who want a calm, organized listing process</li>
        <li>Relocators coordinating from another city or time zone</li>
        <li>Investors evaluating rentals and longer-term holds</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Roots & languages</h2>
      <p>
        Originally from Argentina, Diego brings an international perspective and bilingual service
        (English and Spanish) that helps families feel understood — especially on complex moves.
      </p>
      <h2>How he works</h2>
      <p>
        Expect responsiveness, plain-language updates, and a vendor network for title, inspection,
        and project needs. No template fluff — a clear plan for the next step.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Talk with Diego</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
